\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9.6}{\ignorespaces The scalar residual chain, term by term, on the first-measured ten channels --- the contiguous ATSC allocations 27--36 spanning $z = 1.336$--$1.592$. The reported levels are pilot-derived per-coarse-channel screening values transferred across the $15.36$-bin allocation by the model of Section~\ref {sec:bao:footprint}; they are not direct measurements in every protected bin. No delay-filter credit is claimed (Section~\ref {sec:bao:chain}). ``cap'' marks channels where the correlation-time estimator refused and the chain is evaluated at the sidereal-day bound, so their residuals are upper bounds rather than measurements; $\le $ marks every quantity inheriting such a bound. \emph  {Null frames} is the population from which the kept-frame floor is measured: channels 27, 30, 35, and 36 have none, and channels 28 and 31 have too few to stand on (6 and 2), so their floors are shown parenthesized as indicative and their masked-policy residuals are bounded or blank rather than substituted (channel 28's parenthesized entries inherit the 6-frame floor). $r_{\text  {tol}} = 1.5 \times 10^{-3}$ at the published criterion.}}{91}{table.9.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:bao:channels}{{9.6}{91}{The scalar residual chain, term by term, on the first-measured ten channels --- the contiguous ATSC allocations 27--36 spanning $z = 1.336$--$1.592$. The reported levels are pilot-derived per-coarse-channel screening values transferred across the $15.36$-bin allocation by the model of Section~\ref {sec:bao:footprint}; they are not direct measurements in every protected bin. No delay-filter credit is claimed (Section~\ref {sec:bao:chain}). ``cap'' marks channels where the correlation-time estimator refused and the chain is evaluated at the sidereal-day bound, so their residuals are upper bounds rather than measurements; $\le $ marks every quantity inheriting such a bound. \emph {Null frames} is the population from which the kept-frame floor is measured: channels 27, 30, 35, and 36 have none, and channels 28 and 31 have too few to stand on (6 and 2), so their floors are shown parenthesized as indicative and their masked-policy residuals are bounded or blank rather than substituted (channel 28's parenthesized entries inherit the 6-frame floor). $r_{\text {tol}} = 1.5 \times 10^{-3}$ at the published criterion}{table.9.6}{}}
